Debi joined Savvas in August 2019 as our Employment & Compliance Counsel.  As such, she supports HR and management to ensure compliance with state and federal laws and minimize risk to our employees and Savvas.  Debi also manages the company’s ethics and compliance programs and initiatives.  Debi is here to help so feel free to reach out to her with any questions.    
 
Prior to joining Savvas, Debi was labor and employment counsel at Hertz where she represented the company in matters ranging from labor arbitrations against the Teamsters to discrimination cases before the EEOC.  Prior to being an in-house lawyer, she worked as an employment litigator at a national law firm where she especially enjoyed representing clients willing to go to trial.  Her favorite trial was successfully defending an Atlantic City casino in a lengthy sexual harassment case where she was able to weave in references to her favorite old movies in the closing argument.
 
Outside of Savvas, Debi enjoys planning trips she will take with her family (hopefully soon), visiting as many art museums as possible, cocktails with friends on the front porch of her early 1900’s home, and opera. Although she plans on being at Savvas for many years, she wants to be an art history professor someday.
